    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q30-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $g(x)=\\dfrac{1}{1+2^x}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$g(x)=\\dfrac{2^x\\div2^x}{(2^x+4^x)\\div2^x}=\\dfrac{1}{1+2^x}$.",
          "worked": "Divide the numerator and denominator by $2^x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=\\frac{2^x\\div2^x}{(2^x+4^x)\\div2^x}\\\\g(x)&=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{4^x}{2^x}}\\\\g(x)&=\\frac{1}{1+2^x}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q30-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, sketch the graph of $y=g(x)$.",
