          },
          "worked": "Sketch $y=1+2^x$: it is increasing, passes through $(0,2)$, approaches $y=1$ from above to the left and grows without bound to the right. Apply the reciprocal transformation. The point $(0,2)$ becomes $\\left(0,\\frac12\\right)$. The curve decreases, approaches $y=1$ from below as $x\\to-\\infty$ and approaches $y=0$ from above as $x\\to\\infty$. Since $1+2^x>1$, there are no vertical asymptotes or $x$-intercepts.",
